      "chunkSize": 10,
      "rawToolArgs": "{\"comparisons\":[{\"requirementIndex\":0,\"lemmaName\":\"array_sum\",\"match\":true,\"discrepancy\":\"\",\"weakeningType\":\"none\",\"explanation\":\"The precondition requires equal lengths, and the postconditions specify an output of the same length with each output element equal to the corresponding pair-wise sum.\"},{\"requirementIndex\":1,\"lemmaName\":\"below_zero__ctrl_forall_to_not_exists\",\"match\":false,\"discrepancy\":\"The lemma does not fully guarantee the required boolean behavior. It guarantees that result=true implies some negative cumulative balance and result=false implies all cumulative balances are nonnegative, but it does not guarantee the converse direction that a negative balance forces result=true. Also, the cumulative-sum condition is asserted only through an unquantified negation of an existential, which is equivalent to the expected recurrence, but the result specification remains incomplete.\",\"weakeningType\":\"weakened-postcondition\",\"explanation\":\"The intended requirement is an iff classification: true exactly when any balance falls below zero, false otherwise. The lemma provides only one implication for true and one implication for false; a false result is impossible when a negative balance exists only if the missing converse is established, which it is not.\"},{\"requirementIndex\":2,\"lemmaName\":\"binary_search__ctrl_contrapositive\",\"match\":true,\"discrepancy\":\"\",\"weakeningType\":\"none\",\"explanation\":\"For a sorted array, the bounds and partition conditions characterize the lower-bound index: elements before n are less than key and elements from n onward are at least key. The additional condition rules out returning the array length when some element is not less than key, including the empty-array edge case appropriately.\"},{\"requirementIndex\":3,\"lemmaName\":\"linear_search2__C6\",\"match\":false,\"discrepancy\":\"The postconditions do not require that a[n] equals e, and n is not explicitly constrained to be nonnegative. Thus the lemma does not ensure that the returned index identif...[truncated]"
    }
